//? Title: Faster R-CNN learned proposals and joint training
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A shared-feature detector still needs a way to propose object locations. This report replaces classical proposals with a tensor region proposal network, checks anchor assignment and the full approximate joint Adam loop, and plots selected held-out proposals and detections alongside validation learning curves.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/faster_rcnn.cpp`.

> The method

Faster R-CNN shares image features between an anchor-scoring/refining RPN and a Fast R-CNN head. The training objective sums proposal and region losses. Discrete proposal selection is detached, so the shared backbone receives both tasks while RPN-specific parameters learn from their own targets. The compact source architecture is fitted fully below.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/faster_rcnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/faster_rcnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/faster_rcnn_concept.tikz > build/faster_rcnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/faster_rcnn_concept.svg build/faster_rcnn_concept.dvi > build/faster_rcnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
