> Conclusion

All 1026624 learned scalars are fitted in 160 Adam updates. Validation selects
the last epoch, 5, at AP50 0.414584, and validation AP is still rising, so this
short fit is far from converged. The eight test scenes contain 23 digits: 100 learned
proposals/image cover 1.000000/0.695652 of targets at IoU 0.5/0.7. Final detection
AP50 is 0.308554, AP75 is 0.062168 and AP50:95 is 0.145654, with 249 retained
class-specific detections. The RPN already covers every target at IoU .5 while the
RoI head's classification, refinement and false positives limit AP. The validation/test gap and small
sample preclude an architecture ranking.

The known-anchor fixture establishes assignment geometry, and the visible fit separates proposal learning from region classification/regression. Selected proposal and detection galleries use the same held-out scene pixels, with no ground-truth proposal additions at inference. Metrics describe this bounded digit-scene run; they do not establish the paper's detector accuracy or speed.

> References

- [Ren et al. (2015), Faster R-CNN: Towards Real-Time Object Detection with Region Proposal Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01497).
- [Girshick (2015), Fast R-CNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1504.08083).
- [COCO official box evaluator](https://github.com/cocodataset/cocoapi/blob/master/PythonAPI/pycocotools/cocoeval.py).
